<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Release / App Store build entitlements.

      Differs from Entitlements.plist by exactly ONE key: aps-environment.

        Debug   (Entitlements.plist)        -> "development"
        Release (Entitlements.Release.plist) -> "production"

      Why two files: the Apple Development provisioning profile (used for
      Xcode device builds + simulator) grants aps-environment for the
      sandbox push gateway (api.sandbox.push.apple.com). The Apple
      Distribution / App Store provisioning profile (used for TestFlight
      + App Store) grants it ONLY for the production gateway
      (api.push.apple.com). If the entitlement and the profile disagree,
      MAUI emits warning MT7137 at build time AND Apple's automated
      validation rejects the .ipa upload AND push notifications would
      silently fail in production.

      The Release variant is auto-selected when Configuration=Release
      (see Recto.csproj's CodesignEntitlements conditional). Banked
      2026-05-20 evening during the App Store submission build —
      first Release build surfaced MT7137 because the original
      single-file entitlements was development-only.

      Keychain access group stays explicit on the team-prefixed
      bundle id (same as the Debug file). TEAMID = JVR35HAKZK; if it
      ever changes, BOTH plist files must track it.
    -->
    <key>aps-environment</key>
    <string>production</string>

    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>JVR35HAKZK.app.recto.phone</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
